%% OpenHub -- Session lifecycle (v5)
%% States of an oh session (11-session-interaction §6, ADR-047).
%% Closing the opencode window never stops a session: only "stop" does.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> preparing: oh run / launch form
    preparing --> queued: I6 limit reached<br/>(max active sessions, memory)
    queued --> active: a slot frees up
    preparing --> active: bundle built, server ready,<br/>closed world checked

    state active {
        [*] --> attached
        attached --> detached: last client closed
        detached --> attached: oh session attach
    }

    active --> waiting: decision needed (⏸ ? ! $ ✗)
    waiting --> active: decision taken (first answer wins)
    active --> idle: step finished,<br/>waits for an instruction
    idle --> active: oh session send / prompt
    idle --> sleeping: 5 min, nothing pending<br/>(server stopped)
    sleeping --> active: resume / attach<br/>(same bundle and id)

    active --> completed
    active --> failed
    active --> stopped: oh session stop
    idle --> stopped: oh session stop
    sleeping --> stopped: oh session stop
    completed --> [*]
    failed --> [*]
    stopped --> [*]

    note left of waiting
        ⏸ checkpoint · ? question · ! permission
        $ budget · ✗ error or circuit breaker.
        Answer from oh, opencode, browser or CLI.
    end note

    note right of sleeping
        Quitting oh: idle / waiting sessions sleep now;
        working ones: finish the step then sleep (default),
        keep running in the background, or stop now.
    end note
